<h3>CSS</h3>
<p>The reason that all of the content of this theme is displayed where it is displaying (e.g. position on page) and how it is displaying (colors, font-sizes, etc.) on which pages it is displaying is because of the style.css file and additional files (such as style 1.css). The CSS files are the driving force behind the "look and feel" of a theme.</p>

<p>It is outside the scope of this document to cover CSS comprehensively, but there are some great resources out on the web discussing CSS. Highly recommended is the tutorial course from W3Schools found <a href="http://www.w3schools.com" target="new">here</a>. Having a good working knowledge of CSS will make working with this WordPress theme (or any WordPress theme for that matter) far easier.</p>

<p>This theme uses the <a href="http://lesscss.org/" target="_blank"></a>LESS CSS preprocessor</a> to compile all of the CSS into the. The .less files for the various components of the site can be found in the "less" directory</p>
